Every expense updates the map once, right after it's created — balances are never recomputed from history, only adjusted incrementally.

```text
class BalanceSheet:
    balances: Map<User, Map<User, Money>> = {}   // balances[A][B] = A owes B

    method apply(expense: Expense):
        for split in expense.splits:
            payer = expense.paidBy.anyKeyWithShareFor(split)  // simplified: one payer case
            if split.user == payer:
                continue                      // payer doesn't owe themself
            adjust(split.user, payer, split.amount)

    method adjust(debtor: User, creditor: User, amount: Money):
        // net against any existing opposite-direction debt first
        existing = get(creditor, debtor)
        if existing >= amount:
            decrease(creditor, debtor, amount)
        else:
            decrease(creditor, debtor, existing)
            increase(debtor, creditor, amount - existing)

    method getBalance(a: User, b: User): Money:
        return get(a, b) - get(b, a)
```
